# vi commands with a large count: p and . once put or inserted count
# times, an undo record each time, and on the vos 100000 of them ran
# out of memory for undo. Now . builds its text once, the same text and
# undo (it is one group), as does p when its records would take too
# much of hmem. r and R's ., also built once, undo as before, and r
# keeps each character's kill, the ring's last ten of them.
rc PS1='$ '
rc set -o vi
keys abcd\e0l2x
keys 100000p
keys 0d$\C-l
snap
keys izy\e100000.
keys u\C-l
snap
keys cc0123456789abcdef\e012rxu
snap
keys 012rx$p
snap
keys cc0123456789abcdef\e0Rxy\e3.
snap
keys u
snap
keys \C-l
snap
keys cc\eiecho ok\r
snap
